      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Remainder theorem",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "dividing by \\( (x-r) \\) leaves remainder \\( f(r) \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Factor theorem",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( f(r)=0 \\iff (x-r) \\) is a factor",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Zeros",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "a degree-\\( n \\) polynomial has \\( n \\) zeros (with multiplicity)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 3.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the zeros of \\( f(x)=x^{3}-9x \\).</p><p>Factor out \\( x \\), then a difference of squares:</p>\\[ x(x^{2}-9)=x(x-3)(x+3)=0 \\ \\Rightarrow\\ x=0,\\ 3,\\ -3. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 3.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find the remainder when \\( x^{2}+3x-4 \\) is divided by \\( (x-1) \\).</p><p>By the remainder theorem, evaluate at \\( x=1 \\):</p>\\[ 1+3-4=0. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Show that \\((x-2)\\) is a factor of \\(p(x)=x^3-3x^2+4\\), then fully factorise \\(p(x)\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(p(2)=8-12+4=0\\) ✓. Divide: \\(p(x)=(x-2)(x^2-x-2)=(x-2)(x-2)(x+1)=(x-2)^2(x+1)\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
